rationale:
Owner decision in chat on 2026-09-25. The owner asked to remove the whole agent-branch concept, to delete all branches except main and arena-manager ('branch selain main dan manager-arena boleh dihapus'), to mark the task-distribution issues as no longer valid, and said the Manager itself does the agents' tasks from now on.

Executed so far:
- the 15 other branches were archived as archive/* tags and deleted;
- PR #299 (DEC-0018) was closed unmerged;
- issues #92, #94, #259-#265, #267-#270, #277, #294 and #295 were closed as not planned.

The agent work for TASK-0018 is preserved (tag archive/arena-01a0d83c-n8n-rust-v-4-ff929203) and delivered by the Manager with attribution (DEC-0016 principle).

This also revokes the persistent worker-slot branches of DEC-0003. Its other content stays as history.

Still in force:
- DEC-0014 (one PR per Slice, 8 gates);
- DEC-0015 (runner verification);
- DEC-0009 (Manager credential);
- the milestone register and slice numbering (no new milestone numbers);
- evidence;
- main protection;
- the shared 5 Windows + 5 WSL runner pool.

The legacy workforce engine library under tools/workforce/src (worker-slot model) is no longer used for task distribution. Its removal is a separate follow-up; decisions-check stays.
